<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Icos Vision Systems seeks Nasdaq listing.</title>
<headline>Belgian Icos Vision Systems seeks Nasdaq listing.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Icos Vision Systems, which develops visual monitoring systems for the microchip and security industries, said on Tuesday it was seeking a listing on the U.S. Nasdaq growth stocks market in November.</p>
<p>&quot;November is correct,&quot; chief executive officer Jos Verjans told Reuters in response to a query.</p>
<p>The company hopes to raise $30 million through the operation, he said.</p>
<p>Icos Vision Systems was founded in 1982 as a spin-off from research at Belgium's Leuven university. Management acquired the company with the backing of venture capitalists in 1989.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
